Corrected and recorded as a hard standing rule.

I also explicitly corrected the previous GR↔QM audit status: that presentation may have a local defect or be incomplete, but it is **not `DISCLAIMED`**. Before either negative adjudication or present-day validation, we must:

1. recover the fullest relevant derivation(s), including alternate archive versions;
2. work through the mathematics completely;
3. identify any defects precisely;
4. attempt reasonable mathematical repair;
5. only then assign a validation/disclaimer judgment.

I recorded your directive verbatim in `WORKSPACES/MERIDIAN/LLM_MATH_PROVENANCE_VERIFICATION_PROTOCOL.md`.

One limitation: the runtime does not expose a stable platform turn/message ID to me. Rather than invent one, I recorded the exact locator: **Meridian conversation, 2026-09-19 04:54 -04:00, immediately following RUN_057**, with instructions to append the exported turn ID when recovered.

Commit: `3b9f5c9bea69bf2f5fe42e0568e0af5fee36561d`.

And yes—the next GR↔QM operation changes accordingly: **archive excavation for the working/full calculation before further adjudication.**

